PUBLIC RESPONSE: {}
The three separate Black groups (A2; B3-B4; C1-C2) each have three liberties. Any White move that reduces one group to two liberties still leaves Black able to respond by extending into an open liberty or connecting groups, after which White cannot force the capture in all branches. No single first move therefore initiates a sequence that captures regardless of Black's replies. 

(The shared liberty at B2 is unusable because it is an illegal suicide for White.)

3.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A3}

The relevant black group consists of the connected stones at B3-B4. This group has exactly three liberties: A3, A4 and B2. White's first move at A3 fills one of those liberties and places the group in atari.  

Any subsequent black reply (extending at A4, B2, or elsewhere) can be met by white continuing to fill the remaining liberties in sequence; black never obtains enough additional liberties or eyes to live. All other candidate first moves either fail to reduce the group to one liberty or allow black an escape route that white cannot close regardless of replies. Thus A3 is the unique move that initiates a forced capture.

