6.text:
{B1}

The C1-C2 group has exactly two liberties (B1, B2). B1 places it in atari. After this move B2 becomes an illegal suicide for Black (adjacent stones are A2/B3/C2, all Black, and the single opposing stone at B1 retains its own liberty at A1 so no capture occurs). Black therefore has no legal reply that saves the group; White answers any other Black move by filling B2 on the next turn and removes C1-C2.  

No other first move forces capture against optimal Black defense: A3/A4 leave the B3-B4 group an escape route or eye-forming option, while A1/B2 leave C1-C2 with a remaining liberty that Black can occupy or connect through. Thus only B1 initiates a sequence that captures regardless of Black’s replies.

